-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from ../source/BSMA2004.txt, not from the code.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

-- a motion voted at a meeting, without the 12-week count
GIVEN duly IS A BOOLEAN, days IS A NUMBER, poll IS A BOOLEAN, `for` IS A NUMBER, against IS A NUMBER, `sv for` IS A NUMBER, `sv against` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Motion
`motion` duly days poll `for` against `sv for` `sv against` MEANS
    Motion OF duly, days, poll, `for`, against, `sv for`, `sv against`, 0, 0, 0, FALSE

-- a motion counted 12 weeks on (ss 2(6)-(7))
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER, `sv for` IS A NUMBER, aggregate IS A NUMBER, everyone IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Motion
`motion counted after` weeks `weeks, share value for` `sv for` `of` aggregate `, all in writing:` everyone MEANS
    Motion OF TRUE, 22, TRUE, 0, 0, 0, 0, weeks, `sv for`, aggregate, everyone

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, cap IS A `Candidate capacity`, arrears IS A BOOLEAN, bankrupt IS A BOOLEAN, declared IS A BOOLEAN, office IS A `Council office`, other IS A BOOLEAN, terms IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Candidate
`candidate` age cap arrears bankrupt declared office other terms MEANS
    Candidate OF age, cap, arrears, FALSE, FALSE, bankrupt, declared, other, office, terms

`a plain proprietor` MEANS `candidate` 40 `a subsidiary proprietor` FALSE FALSE FALSE `an ordinary member` FALSE 0

GIVEN due IS A DATE, paid IS A MAYBE DATE, demand IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Contribution facts`
`contribution due` due `, paid` paid `, demand` demand MEANS `Contribution facts` OF due, paid, demand, FALSE

GIVEN made IS A DATE, months IS A NUMBER, requested IS A MAYBE DATE, decided IS A BOOLEAN, renewed IS A BOOLEAN, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Interim order facts`
`interim order` made months requested decided renewed `as at` MEANS `Interim order facts` OF made, months, requested, decided, renewed, `as at`

§§ `Goal 1 — the six resolutions (s 2)`

-- s 2(2): ordinary — 15th day, more for than against
#ASSERT `the motion is decided as` `an ordinary resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 15 FALSE 10 9 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `an ordinary resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 14 FALSE 10 9 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `an ordinary resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 15 FALSE 10 10 0 0)
-- on a poll, share value decides: 10 heads for, 2 against, but 500 to 600 by value
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `an ordinary resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 15 TRUE 10 2 500 600)
-- s 2(3): special — 22nd day, at least 75% of the value of valid votes cast
#ASSERT `the motion is decided as` `a special resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 TRUE 3 1 750 250)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a special resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 TRUE 3 1 749 251)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a special resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 21 TRUE 3 1 750 250)
-- s 2(5): 90%
#ASSERT `the motion is decided as` `a 90% resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 TRUE 9 1 900 100)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a 90% resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 TRUE 9 1 899 101)
-- s 2(4): unanimous — every valid vote cast
#ASSERT `the motion is decided as` `a unanimous resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 FALSE 5 0 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a unanimous resolution` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 FALSE 5 1 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a unanimous resolution` `, on` (`motion` FALSE 22 FALSE 5 0 0 0)
-- s 2(6): comprehensive — 90% of ALL proprietors' share value, 12 weeks on
#ASSERT `the motion is decided as` `a comprehensive resolution` `, on` (`motion counted after` 12 `weeks, share value for` 900 `of` 1000 `, all in writing:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a comprehensive resolution` `, on` (`motion counted after` 11 `weeks, share value for` 900 `of` 1000 `, all in writing:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a comprehensive resolution` `, on` (`motion counted after` 12 `weeks, share value for` 899 `of` 1000 `, all in writing:` FALSE)
-- s 2(7): by consensus — every proprietor in writing, 12 weeks on
#ASSERT `the motion is decided as` `a resolution by consensus` `, on` (`motion counted after` 12 `weeks, share value for` 0 `of` 1000 `, all in writing:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the motion is decided as` `a resolution by consensus` `, on` (`motion counted after` 12 `weeks, share value for` 999 `of` 1000 `, all in writing:` FALSE)
-- First Schedule para 9(4): a proposed lot's vote is worth 25%, fraction ignored
#ASSERT `the value of the vote, share value` 10 `, a proposed lot:` TRUE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the value of the vote, share value` 10 `, a proposed lot:` FALSE EQUALS 10

§§ `Goal 1 — which resolution each matter needs`

#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` (`an exclusive use by-law` 1) EQUALS `an ordinary resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` (`an exclusive use by-law` 2) EQUALS `a special resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` (`an exclusive use by-law` 3) EQUALS `a special resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` (`an exclusive use by-law` 3.5) EQUALS `a 90% resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` (`leasing common property` 4) EQUALS `a 90% resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` (`leasing common property for a fixed EV charger` 10) EQUALS `an ordinary resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `granting, accepting or surrendering an easement or restrictive covenant (s 35)` EQUALS `a unanimous resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `making, amending or repealing by-laws (s 32(3))` EQUALS `a special resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `a by-law for parking lots with fixed EV chargers (s 32(3A))` EQUALS `an ordinary resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `authorising an improvement increasing floor area (s 37(2))` EQUALS `a 90% resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `terminating the strata scheme (s 84(1))` EQUALS `a resolution by consensus`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `levying contributions by a different formula after a change of use (s 41(6))` EQUALS `a comprehensive resolution`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `not insuring the building under a damage policy (s 70(1))` EQUALS `a resolution by consensus`
#ASSERT `the resolution needed for` `transferring common property (s 34(1)(a))` EQUALS `a 90% resolution`
#ASSERT `the matter is validly decided:` `granting, accepting or surrendering an easement or restrictive covenant (s 35)` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 22 FALSE 5 0 0 0)
-- a bare majority at 15 days is not a special resolution for a by-law
#ASSERT NOT `the matter is validly decided:` `making, amending or repealing by-laws (s 32(3))` `, on` (`motion` TRUE 15 FALSE 6 5 0 0)
#ASSERT `the resolution needed to amend or revoke a` `a special resolution` EQUALS `a special resolution`

